            <div xml:id="d232">

                <pb facs="0277" n="265" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg265"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.5111/672: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Deputy Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>(<hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>) <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Bordeaux</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-22T17:00:00+02:00">June 22, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>72. For the President. Reynaud is deeply touched by your personal message and
                    asks me to convey to you an expression of his profound appreciation. He is happy
                    thus to learn that you are aware of his fight to continue resistance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Biddle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
